WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.238 --> 00:00:01.773
- I was not interested in music.

00:00:01.773 --> 00:00:04.092
I was really trying to be
the next Michael Jordan,

00:00:04.092 --> 00:00:04.925
of course.

00:00:04.925 --> 00:00:09.092
I look at my music like a
soldier looks at his sword.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:16.206
Never put your sword down
in the midst of a war.

00:00:16.206 --> 00:00:18.654
I'm not that guy that say,
man, this music's dead.

00:00:18.654 --> 00:00:19.487
It ain't nothing,

00:00:19.487 --> 00:00:21.144
it ain't nothing like it used to be like.

00:00:21.144 --> 00:00:22.325
That's when you're old.

00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:23.287
That's when you're outdated.

00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:24.938
I'm not in no lane.

00:00:24.938 --> 00:00:27.524
The Earth is my turf when
it comes to this music.

00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:28.357
- That's a--

00:00:28.357 --> 00:00:31.014
- He's an American singer,
songwriter, record producer,

00:00:31.014 --> 00:00:33.581
and former professional basketball player.

00:00:33.581 --> 00:00:36.057
He's recognized as one of
the bestselling music artists

00:00:36.057 --> 00:00:39.749
in the United States, with
over 40 million albums sold.

00:00:39.749 --> 00:00:43.118
He's been credited with helping
redefine R&amp;B and hip hop,

00:00:43.118 --> 00:00:45.670
earning the name, The King of R&amp;B.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.231
He's R. Kelly, and here's my take

00:00:47.231 --> 00:00:49.276
on his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:49.276 --> 00:00:50.900
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.163
and I'm curious to figure out which one

00:00:52.163 --> 00:00:54.146
you guys like the best, and as always,

00:00:54.146 --> 00:00:56.639
as he's talking, if he says
something that really sticks out

00:00:56.639 --> 00:00:58.657
and is meaningful to
you, please write it down

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:00.343
in the comments below
and put quotes around it,

00:01:00.343 --> 00:01:03.072
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:01:03.072 --> 00:01:03.905
Enjoy!

00:01:07.126 --> 00:01:10.376
(soft thrilling music)

00:01:17.263 --> 00:01:19.201
- I believe that the depth
of anybody's struggle

00:01:19.201 --> 00:01:21.447
will determine the
height of their success.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.752
And I believe that everything
that I've gone through

00:01:23.752 --> 00:01:26.569
in my whole life, you know, people ask me,

00:01:26.569 --> 00:01:27.547
what would you change?

00:01:27.547 --> 00:01:29.562
I wouldn't change a
thing because everything

00:01:29.562 --> 00:01:32.100
that I've gone through has
made me who I am today.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.008
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:01:33.008 --> 00:01:36.462
So I'm sitting here very
strong and very confident,

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:39.792
and it got a lot of love
for a lot of, lot of people.

00:01:39.792 --> 00:01:41.733
Jesus struggled and went through things.

00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:43.672
Everybody went through their own thing,

00:01:43.672 --> 00:01:46.770
and people were slandering him, I mean,

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.289
I feel like if Jesus can
go what he went through,

00:01:49.289 --> 00:01:50.729
who am I?

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:52.306
(audience shouting)
(laughing)

00:01:52.306 --> 00:01:53.596
I'm nobody.

00:01:53.596 --> 00:01:55.346
You know what I'm saying,
just a guy from the hood, man,

00:01:55.346 --> 00:01:57.707
that just do this music, you know,

00:01:57.707 --> 00:01:59.224
but I'm just such a real person.

00:01:59.224 --> 00:02:01.692
I don't consider myself
a celebrity at all.

00:02:01.692 --> 00:02:03.307
I'm just so real and I love people

00:02:03.307 --> 00:02:05.964
that, man, I just float
through this thing,

00:02:05.964 --> 00:02:08.038
and I let my music, I let God guide me

00:02:08.038 --> 00:02:10.667
where he got me to go, but God
ain't going to just guide you

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:13.229
straight to success, not God.

00:02:13.229 --> 00:02:15.930
He gon' guide you through
a lot of mess first.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.318
So then when you get the success

00:02:17.318 --> 00:02:18.588
you'll know how to appreciate it

00:02:18.588 --> 00:02:20.332
and you'll know how to stay with it,

00:02:20.332 --> 00:02:21.736
and know how to take care of it,

00:02:21.736 --> 00:02:24.519
and that's called longevity.

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:25.593
- [Interviewer] And I
know about your school.

00:02:25.593 --> 00:02:26.895
And I know about a certain lady

00:02:26.895 --> 00:02:30.216
that I'd like you to tell
us about who inspired you

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.833
and encouraged you to do music.

00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:34.191
Can you tell us a bit about her?

00:02:34.191 --> 00:02:36.875
- Well that's Lena McLin,
like my second mother,

00:02:36.875 --> 00:02:39.243
and she's a pastor, and everything,

00:02:39.243 --> 00:02:41.910
my music teacher in high school.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:46.411
In high school, my freshman
year, I was starting on

00:02:46.411 --> 00:02:48.000
Kenwood's basketball team,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.502
which is the name of my high school.

00:02:50.502 --> 00:02:53.022
But I happened to have a music class.

00:02:53.022 --> 00:02:56.168
At that point in time I
think I was about 16, 17,

00:02:56.168 --> 00:02:58.570
I was not interested in music,

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:03.449
I was really trying to be the
next Michael Jordan of course.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.267
She told me that I would sing,

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:10.984
I would be the next Stevie
Wonder, or superstar,

00:03:10.984 --> 00:03:13.159
Michael Jackson, or something like that.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:15.402
And I laughed at her like
she was crazy you know,

00:03:15.402 --> 00:03:18.294
I was, I couldn't see it.

00:03:18.294 --> 00:03:20.197
Everything I am today she could see it,

00:03:20.197 --> 00:03:22.052
my mother could see it,

00:03:22.052 --> 00:03:23.063
and she would tell me

00:03:23.063 --> 00:03:27.353
that I was going to be where
I'm at today, and even further.

00:03:27.353 --> 00:03:29.468
And it just happened.

00:03:29.468 --> 00:03:32.976
She put me in a talent show,
and I did the talent show,

00:03:32.976 --> 00:03:35.344
and the girls was
screaming and everything,

00:03:35.344 --> 00:03:36.283
and I was like man,

00:03:36.283 --> 00:03:39.258
I don't get this kind
of love on the court,

00:03:39.258 --> 00:03:41.762
(laughing) you know.

00:03:41.762 --> 00:03:45.398
And of course I'm going to
chose that over basketball,

00:03:45.398 --> 00:03:47.434
and I did, and I've been
doing it ever since.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:49.462
- [Interviewer] So would you
say that was your big break,

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.427
or was there a stage a
little further down the line

00:03:51.427 --> 00:03:55.770
that was a significant
break for your music?

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:58.672
- I would say my big break
is that point in time

00:03:58.672 --> 00:04:01.505
I learned that Stevie Wonder riff.

00:04:02.774 --> 00:04:05.232
That was one of the
steps 'cause I felt like

00:04:05.232 --> 00:04:07.073
if I learned that I can learn anything,

00:04:07.073 --> 00:04:09.956
'cause that guy was going pretty fast.

00:04:09.956 --> 00:04:14.489
But, as far as crowd
wise and what nailed it,

00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:17.369
I would say my first talent show

00:04:17.369 --> 00:04:18.952
pretty much is what

00:04:20.177 --> 00:04:22.010
bit me in a way, like,

00:04:23.206 --> 00:04:26.510
Peter Parker got bit by the
spider and became Spiderman,

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.346
that was the bite for me.

00:04:28.346 --> 00:04:30.925
When the women and
everybody was showing me

00:04:30.925 --> 00:04:33.953
so much love at the talent show and I won,

00:04:33.953 --> 00:04:37.187
and I was like wow, it was overwhelming.

00:04:37.187 --> 00:04:39.163
Four years I street performed here

00:04:39.163 --> 00:04:40.974
before I got my record deal.

00:04:40.974 --> 00:04:45.422
I was on the streets with
a little bitty keyboard.

00:04:45.422 --> 00:04:46.332
- Okay.

00:04:46.332 --> 00:04:50.579
- With glasses on like
I was Stevie Wonder.

00:04:50.579 --> 00:04:51.973
You know.

00:04:51.973 --> 00:04:53.359
Hustling, you know.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.738
With a big chitlin bucket,

00:04:55.738 --> 00:05:00.465
I paid my rent and my mom's
rent off of street performing.

00:05:00.465 --> 00:05:03.380
But I would only do it
three days out of the week.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.563
Just three days, but I would
be uh I can't talk no more,

00:05:06.563 --> 00:05:07.587
I can't even talk,

00:05:07.587 --> 00:05:12.116
'cause I was like singing for
like eight hours straight,

00:05:12.116 --> 00:05:14.585
for people going to work
and coming from work.

00:05:14.585 --> 00:05:16.679
(soft music)

00:05:16.679 --> 00:05:21.543
Then I hitchhiked to LA
but I lived on the beach.

00:05:21.543 --> 00:05:22.710
Cardboard box,

00:05:23.687 --> 00:05:26.354
and big beach towels I slept on.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:28.771
- In the beach?

00:05:28.771 --> 00:05:31.421
- On the beach, everyday.

00:05:31.421 --> 00:05:33.254
Then I'd wake back up.

00:05:34.724 --> 00:05:37.391
When I'd wake up I'd sing again.

00:05:38.626 --> 00:05:41.526
Then I came, I hitchhiked back to Chicago,

00:05:41.526 --> 00:05:42.762
and then I got discovered.

00:05:42.762 --> 00:05:45.464
But I did all that for like
six years, street performing.

00:05:45.464 --> 00:05:48.890
- [Interviewer] What is your secret?

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:50.828
- Just being very observant, you know.

00:05:50.828 --> 00:05:53.491
I'm very observant of people

00:05:53.491 --> 00:05:58.241
and my mom always taught me
don't write songs, write life.

00:05:58.241 --> 00:06:00.403
You know, and only way
you're going to write life

00:06:00.403 --> 00:06:02.086
is that you'll be very
observant of people,

00:06:02.086 --> 00:06:03.603
and always paying attention to people

00:06:03.603 --> 00:06:06.372
and the needs of people
and what they talking about

00:06:06.372 --> 00:06:07.967
these days, you know.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:11.716
And then kind of like
challenging that into your gift,

00:06:11.716 --> 00:06:12.719
which is my music.

00:06:12.719 --> 00:06:15.812
And I believe that I
long as I continue to be

00:06:15.812 --> 00:06:18.591
observant of people and
do that, I'll be alright.

00:06:18.591 --> 00:06:22.508
- The seven year turmoil
that you went through,

00:06:23.538 --> 00:06:27.170
vis-a-vis the trial for child pornography,

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:30.300
your advisors almost to a person,

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.288
told you over and over and over again

00:06:32.288 --> 00:06:34.101
while you're going through this period,

00:06:34.101 --> 00:06:37.649
Kells, do not put out
sexually explicit material.

00:06:37.649 --> 00:06:40.600
Do not, the audience can't handle that,

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.087
your fans can't handle
it, it's not gon' be good

00:06:43.087 --> 00:06:45.926
for the outcome of this
trial, tone it down,

00:06:45.926 --> 00:06:47.106
don't put that out.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:51.273
You ignore all of 'em, do it
anyway, and get bold with it.

00:06:52.587 --> 00:06:55.287
It's during this period you
put out Chocolate Factory,

00:06:55.287 --> 00:06:57.794
you put our Remix, you put out Ignition.

00:06:57.794 --> 00:06:59.670
Here they are telling you not to do this

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:00.907
and you put out a song about

00:07:00.907 --> 00:07:03.049
putting your key in the ignition.

00:07:03.049 --> 00:07:05.221
I read that, and I
wanted to ask, so I will,

00:07:05.221 --> 00:07:08.610
why it is that you went
against your advisors,

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.992
what is it that you were
thinking, that you were feeling,

00:07:10.992 --> 00:07:14.081
that kept you doing that
when everybody else told you

00:07:14.081 --> 00:07:15.806
not to do that.

00:07:15.806 --> 00:07:18.659
- Well first of all let me say, you know,

00:07:18.659 --> 00:07:20.745
I wasn't bold about it,

00:07:20.745 --> 00:07:22.605
and I didn't totally ignore 'em,

00:07:22.605 --> 00:07:23.983
because that would be
the worst thing to do,

00:07:23.983 --> 00:07:27.163
is totally ignore your
advisors or your lawyers.

00:07:27.163 --> 00:07:31.461
I listened to 'em, we talked,
we discussed the situation,

00:07:31.461 --> 00:07:35.628
I felt strong, very strong,
as I said many years ago

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:38.027
about the trial,

00:07:38.027 --> 00:07:40.725
that I will have my day in court,

00:07:40.725 --> 00:07:44.095
and I will be innocent,
and I will walk away,

00:07:44.095 --> 00:07:46.135
and I will move on with my life.

00:07:46.135 --> 00:07:48.065
I said that in the beginning,

00:07:48.065 --> 00:07:49.279
I said that during the middle

00:07:49.279 --> 00:07:51.963
part of the trial and everything else.

00:07:51.963 --> 00:07:56.130
I look at my music like a
soldier looks at his sword.

00:08:00.122 --> 00:08:04.285
Never put your sword down
in the midst of a war.

00:08:04.285 --> 00:08:08.025
You never lay down in the midst of a war.

00:08:08.025 --> 00:08:10.707
And I think that my lawyers

00:08:10.707 --> 00:08:13.036
were good lawyers, great lawyers,

00:08:13.036 --> 00:08:16.132
but I didn't think they
had that part down.

00:08:16.132 --> 00:08:19.460
And you have to be the soldier
in the midst of the war

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.460
to even understand that.

00:08:22.421 --> 00:08:25.884
And I was the soldier on the front line,

00:08:25.884 --> 00:08:29.551
for my life, for my
kid's life, for my fans.

00:08:31.257 --> 00:08:34.340
And I told them I would not lay down.

00:08:36.561 --> 00:08:38.978
I would not stop doing music.

00:08:39.966 --> 00:08:41.575
Why would I do that?

00:08:41.575 --> 00:08:43.930
I think that would say,
oh yeah, he did it.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.844
I think that would say all of the things

00:08:45.844 --> 00:08:49.094
that people want to say about R. Kelly.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:53.312
So I did what I'm supposed to do.

00:08:53.312 --> 00:08:55.483
Like any fireman that
goes up in the building,

00:08:55.483 --> 00:08:57.877
they don't get to the
building say oh wait a minute,

00:08:57.877 --> 00:09:00.044
that's just too much fire.

00:09:01.377 --> 00:09:05.892
But you're a fireman, so
go and fight the fire.

00:09:05.892 --> 00:09:07.185
Don't care how much it is.

00:09:07.185 --> 00:09:10.484
I had to go and I had to do my music.

00:09:10.484 --> 00:09:15.180
I'm not going to change my lyric,
I'm not going to change my name,

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:16.478
I'm not going to do any of that.

00:09:16.478 --> 00:09:18.623
I'm going to do my music,
and that's what I did,

00:09:18.623 --> 00:09:19.901
and that's what I told the company,

00:09:19.901 --> 00:09:22.456
even though they continued
to say no, don't do it.

00:09:22.456 --> 00:09:25.782
But the minute ignition came out,

00:09:25.782 --> 00:09:28.794
which was the first
song I did, it blew up,

00:09:28.794 --> 00:09:30.346
and all of sudden the
company's calling me,

00:09:30.346 --> 00:09:32.330
everybody's calling me, come
do an album cover shoot,

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:33.558
we got to get the rest of this album done,

00:09:33.558 --> 00:09:34.730
we got to go there, we got to run,

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:35.749
do what you do, what you got to do,

00:09:35.749 --> 00:09:36.923
bring your clothes, we gon' have a,

00:09:36.923 --> 00:09:39.093
well I ain't got no doggone makeup person.

00:09:39.093 --> 00:09:40.420
You got some makeup,
bring your own makeup,

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:41.253
we'll do it all.

00:09:41.253 --> 00:09:42.972
I mean, it just got crazy.

00:09:42.972 --> 00:09:45.510
So I did what I felt was right.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:47.843
I started saying things like

00:09:51.076 --> 00:09:55.243
♫ I can hear someone over
there calling me oh who

00:09:58.007 --> 00:09:59.665
The crowd would just go crazy.

00:09:59.665 --> 00:10:01.168
And then I walk down there.

00:10:01.168 --> 00:10:05.335
♫ I can hear someone
over there calling me oh

00:10:06.957 --> 00:10:08.261
And they'd go crazy,

00:10:08.261 --> 00:10:11.928
this before Body Calling
was even, was born.

00:10:13.162 --> 00:10:14.899
Little gimmicks like that,

00:10:14.899 --> 00:10:17.384
and oh na, na, na, na, na.

00:10:17.384 --> 00:10:20.351
Crowd go, your body, na, na.

00:10:20.351 --> 00:10:23.163
And it was just amazing, little
gimmicks that I was doing

00:10:23.163 --> 00:10:24.080
on my show.

00:10:24.919 --> 00:10:26.881
I never thought that I would
take it into the studio

00:10:26.881 --> 00:10:28.477
and say okay Ima make a whole song

00:10:28.477 --> 00:10:31.201
out of your body calling,
Your Body's Calling Me.

00:10:31.201 --> 00:10:34.368
But that's how these songs came about.

00:10:36.448 --> 00:10:38.288
The more I started doing that,

00:10:38.288 --> 00:10:39.915
the more I started deciding well

00:10:39.915 --> 00:10:42.329
I'm just going to start
saying what I feel,

00:10:42.329 --> 00:10:44.055
'cause I would always say on my stage

00:10:44.055 --> 00:10:47.296
♫ Do you mind if I say
what I feel right now

00:10:47.296 --> 00:10:48.497
They would love it.

00:10:48.497 --> 00:10:50.387
Then I'd say what I feel.

00:10:50.387 --> 00:10:53.341
♫ Say I'm feeling kind of horny right now

00:10:53.341 --> 00:10:54.846
And they would snap, you know.

00:10:54.846 --> 00:10:56.375
But that's what I would feel.

00:10:56.375 --> 00:10:57.525
And I say what I feel,

00:10:57.525 --> 00:11:00.851
people appreciate me
keeping it real with 'em.

00:11:00.851 --> 00:11:04.204
And everybody wants to
know what you really feel,

00:11:04.204 --> 00:11:05.780
that's when you're known.

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:07.824
They want to know what
you're really thinking.

00:11:07.824 --> 00:11:10.097
So I was giving them what was on my mind

00:11:10.097 --> 00:11:12.045
and on my heart at that particular time.

00:11:12.045 --> 00:11:13.993
- [Interviewer] You reckon
you found your niche there,

00:11:13.993 --> 00:11:15.765
really, at that point.

00:11:15.765 --> 00:11:19.092
I mean everybody, a lot of R&amp;B artists,

00:11:19.092 --> 00:11:21.209
were trying to do that kind of thing,

00:11:21.209 --> 00:11:23.568
but you kind of did it
just that bit better.

00:11:23.568 --> 00:11:25.383
- Well I think it's because

00:11:25.383 --> 00:11:26.485
after I started doing it

00:11:26.485 --> 00:11:29.506
a lot of people would
follow, if you don't mind,

00:11:29.506 --> 00:11:31.033
I mean a lot of people would follow,

00:11:31.033 --> 00:11:32.406
in a humble way I say that.

00:11:32.406 --> 00:11:36.406
But you know it's a
difference when you mean it.

00:11:37.676 --> 00:11:39.392
You know, you do it.

00:11:39.392 --> 00:11:43.158
When I came up with it, it
came out of me from my belly.

00:11:43.158 --> 00:11:45.714
And I did it because that's what I felt,

00:11:45.714 --> 00:11:47.408
and that's what was on my mind.

00:11:47.408 --> 00:11:51.044
A lot of other people, when they did it,

00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:52.641
they were inspired to do it.

00:11:52.641 --> 00:11:54.950
And it's a difference, you
know, it's a difference

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:59.900
in who created the light bulb,
and then who turned it on,

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:01.420
it's a big difference.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:02.370
The music is still in me,

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.017
and it's more powerful
now than it's ever been,

00:12:05.017 --> 00:12:06.069
because I don't know,

00:12:06.069 --> 00:12:08.054
it's something Benjamin Button about me.

00:12:08.054 --> 00:12:10.151
I don't know really what it is,

00:12:10.151 --> 00:12:11.591
it's just the weirdest thing in the world.

00:12:11.591 --> 00:12:14.910
I love music and I keep
my ears close to music,

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.871
and I'm always studying the new artists.

00:12:16.871 --> 00:12:18.591
I'm not that guy that say,

00:12:18.591 --> 00:12:20.160
man this music today it ain't nothing,

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:22.257
it ain't nothing like it used to be like.

00:12:22.257 --> 00:12:24.205
That's when you're old,
that's when you're outdated,

00:12:24.205 --> 00:12:27.318
but when you can appreciate the newcomers

00:12:27.318 --> 00:12:29.797
as well as you can appreciate
the Stevie Wonders,

00:12:29.797 --> 00:12:32.254
and the Sam Cookes all in one,

00:12:32.254 --> 00:12:33.238
you kind of stay fresh,

00:12:33.238 --> 00:12:35.657
and you kind of stay
up on what's going on,

00:12:35.657 --> 00:12:37.692
and you can be able to
study it and continue

00:12:37.692 --> 00:12:38.953
to upgrade yourself.

00:12:38.953 --> 00:12:40.629
You know, no different than the iPhone.

00:12:40.629 --> 00:12:42.934
Comes with different apps
and different new things.

00:12:42.934 --> 00:12:46.170
And that's what I like
to consider myself as.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:48.864
- Do you have one set process
in how you make a song

00:12:48.864 --> 00:12:51.287
or is it different with
you every single time.

00:12:51.287 --> 00:12:52.731
- It's different every single time,

00:12:52.731 --> 00:12:54.921
but at the same time, you know,

00:12:54.921 --> 00:12:57.693
I believe in keeping it real.

00:12:57.693 --> 00:12:59.861
And when I'm singing on these tracks

00:12:59.861 --> 00:13:03.156
I don't really write the
song, I let it write me.

00:13:03.156 --> 00:13:04.368
So whatever it tells me to say,

00:13:04.368 --> 00:13:06.751
if it say hey, say feeling on your booty.

00:13:06.751 --> 00:13:07.847
(laughing)

00:13:07.847 --> 00:13:09.779
♫ Feeling on your booty

00:13:09.779 --> 00:13:10.612
I'm just gon' say it.
(audience cheering)

00:13:10.612 --> 00:13:12.005
- Sing it Kells, sing it!

00:13:12.005 --> 00:13:13.849
- You know, if it tell me to go,

00:13:13.849 --> 00:13:15.198
say I know this gon' sound stupid,

00:13:15.198 --> 00:13:17.306
but say bugabugabuga, okay.

00:13:17.306 --> 00:13:20.322
♫ Bugabugabugabugabugatee

00:13:20.322 --> 00:13:22.513
I'm not, you know.

00:13:22.513 --> 00:13:23.740
I'm just gon' keep it real, you know,

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:24.573
I'm a keep it real,

00:13:24.573 --> 00:13:26.132
'cause if that's what
the music tell me to do,

00:13:26.132 --> 00:13:27.120
that's what Ima.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.074
Well not to promote it too fast,

00:13:29.074 --> 00:13:32.407
but my book is called R. Kelly No Lanes.

00:13:33.474 --> 00:13:36.693
And what that means
is, I'm not in no lane.

00:13:36.693 --> 00:13:38.869
The Earth is my turf when
it comes to this music.

00:13:38.869 --> 00:13:40.167
- That's a book you put out.

00:13:40.167 --> 00:13:41.000
- Yeah.
- Another book?

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.037
- You know it's R. Kelly, No Lanes.

00:13:43.037 --> 00:13:45.157
And because you get put in a lane,

00:13:45.157 --> 00:13:46.202
and if you stay one lane man

00:13:46.202 --> 00:13:48.697
that's just really where you gon' go.

00:13:48.697 --> 00:13:50.960
That one lane gon' lead you to one place.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.982
Ain't no particular
address that I'm going to,

00:13:52.982 --> 00:13:56.708
ain't no particular street
I want to ride on, you know.

00:13:56.708 --> 00:13:58.684
And like I say Earth is my turf,

00:13:58.684 --> 00:14:01.521
and that's my story
and I'm sticking to it.

00:14:01.521 --> 00:14:05.661
I had all of his music,
posters, everything up,

00:14:05.661 --> 00:14:08.959
I had Moonwalker playing
on the video screen.

00:14:08.959 --> 00:14:11.126
And I would just go for the song.

00:14:11.126 --> 00:14:12.059
As I look at Mike,

00:14:12.059 --> 00:14:14.211
I would sing what I thought he would sing.

00:14:14.211 --> 00:14:16.891
You know, I was just mimicking
what I thought he would say

00:14:16.891 --> 00:14:18.581
on the lyrics and everything.

00:14:18.581 --> 00:14:20.021
And then when he asked me,

00:14:20.021 --> 00:14:21.482
is there you anyway you can come in here

00:14:21.482 --> 00:14:24.232
and sing the backgrounds with me.

00:14:25.405 --> 00:14:26.972
I was like uh.

00:14:26.972 --> 00:14:29.222
(laughing)

00:14:30.113 --> 00:14:32.998
Sure, uh yeah, of course, why not.

00:14:32.998 --> 00:14:34.343
Yeah, I'll be in there
in a minute, you know.

00:14:34.343 --> 00:14:35.182
(laughing)

00:14:35.182 --> 00:14:36.385
And I walked out,

00:14:36.385 --> 00:14:38.705
and I got between the
wall that he couldn't see.

00:14:38.705 --> 00:14:40.250
And I was like.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.772
(laughing)

00:14:42.772 --> 00:14:43.605
Damn.

00:14:44.721 --> 00:14:46.104
I'm finna mess up.

00:14:46.104 --> 00:14:47.249
I thought I was gon' go in there

00:14:47.249 --> 00:14:48.150
and just like a little girl man,

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:49.535
and just mess it up.

00:14:49.535 --> 00:14:51.275
But we standing there, he,

00:14:51.275 --> 00:14:54.282
♫ You are not alone

00:14:54.282 --> 00:14:57.002
♫ I am here with you

00:14:57.002 --> 00:14:58.575
And all I got to do
really, I'm telling myself,

00:14:58.575 --> 00:15:01.870
sing what you sang on the demo, you idiot.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:02.848
And you can't go wrong

00:15:02.848 --> 00:15:05.126
'cause you sounding like
Michael on it anyway.

00:15:05.126 --> 00:15:08.547
So I'm doing that, and
I'm he's here, right here,

00:15:08.547 --> 00:15:11.656
at the same mic, we
both got on headphones,

00:15:11.656 --> 00:15:13.214
and I'm going

00:15:13.214 --> 00:15:16.584
♫ You are not alone

00:15:16.584 --> 00:15:17.752
He would look over at me, I'll be like,

00:15:17.752 --> 00:15:20.833
♫ I am here with you

00:15:20.833 --> 00:15:23.657
♫ Though you're far away

00:15:23.657 --> 00:15:26.981
♫ I am here to stay

00:15:26.981 --> 00:15:30.306
♫ You are not alone

00:15:30.306 --> 00:15:31.892
And you know he got that
little shake in his voice,

00:15:31.892 --> 00:15:34.460
man I was like, oh, I was just blown away.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:37.633
I'm standing here singing
with Michael Jackson.

00:15:37.633 --> 00:15:40.001
Right here, I'm right here.

00:15:40.001 --> 00:15:42.191
I'm starting to grab his hand,
but I ain't want to do that,

00:15:42.191 --> 00:15:44.858
I ain't want to do that, you know.

00:15:46.337 --> 00:15:49.249
We'll just sing We Are The
World, this You Are Not Alone,

00:15:49.249 --> 00:15:50.296
don't do it.

00:15:50.296 --> 00:15:52.181
So I started to grab his hand, and just,

00:15:52.181 --> 00:15:55.066
just for good measure you
know, but I ain't do that.

00:15:55.066 --> 00:15:57.618
But it was a great time
working with Michael man.

00:15:57.618 --> 00:15:58.920
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:01.708
I made this video because
Ruby Watson asked me to.

00:16:01.708 --> 00:16:02.884
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:16:02.884 --> 00:16:04.380
that you want me to profile next,

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.810
leave it down in the comments below

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.137
and I'll see what I can do.

00:16:07.137 --> 00:16:09.522
I'd also love to know what
was the biggest lesson

00:16:09.522 --> 00:16:11.006
that you learned from this video

00:16:11.006 --> 00:16:13.434
that you're going to
immediately apply to your life

00:16:13.434 --> 00:16:14.367
for your business.

00:16:14.367 --> 00:16:15.560
Leave it in the comments,

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:17.095
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:16:17.095 --> 00:16:19.332
Finally, I wanted to give a
quick shout out to Ariel Ziv,

00:16:19.332 --> 00:16:21.458
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:16:21.458 --> 00:16:22.405
Your One Word,

00:16:22.405 --> 00:16:24.755
and then flying to Toronto to meet me,

00:16:24.755 --> 00:16:26.111
to get it signed.

00:16:26.111 --> 00:16:28.143
That was a fun day, I
really appreciate it.

00:16:28.143 --> 00:16:29.404
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:16:29.404 --> 00:16:30.517
I believe in you,

00:16:30.517 --> 00:16:32.805
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:16:32.805 --> 00:16:34.840
and whatever your one word is.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:37.257
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:16:38.267 --> 00:16:40.521
(thrilling music)

